{
  "body_human_readable": "## \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Movie: By the Numbers\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction novel, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of approximately $104.5 million.\n\nThe film, directed by Garth Jennings, was released in the United Kingdom on April 28, 2005, and a day later in North America. In its opening weekend in the United States, it secured the top spot at the box office, earning $21.1 million. The worldwide box office total was $104,478,416.\n\nThe domestic gross in the United States accounted for $51,085,416, with international markets contributing $53,393,000 to the film's total earnings. Despite earning back its production costs, the film's performance was not considered strong enough to warrant a sequel.",
